3454 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (While designing this recurring bill payment flow, my primary focus was to create an experience that feels simple, secure, and trustworthy for users. Since recurring payments involve automatic money deductions, I wanted users to feel fully informed and in control at every step.\n\nI structured the flow in a step-by-step manner to reduce confusion and make navigation intuitive, especially for users who may not be familiar with AutoPay features. I also tried to minimize manual effort by assuming that biller information and consumer details could already be available from previous bill payments.\n\nSpecial attention was given to user trust and error prevention. This is why the flow includes review screens, PIN verification, validation states, and support options such as FAQs and Contact Support. I also included management features so users can later pause, edit, or cancel recurring payments easily.\n\nAccessibility and clarity were considered throughout the design by using clear labels, readable layouts, simple language, and large touch-friendly elements to ensure the experience remains inclusive and easy to use.)
/K [104]
/S /Span
/Type /StructElem
/P 3455 0 R
/Pg 1455 0 R
>>
endobj
